    "result_text": "The full suite is green: **271 tests, 0 failures, 0 errors**.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented telephone normalization so numbers are stored and compared as digits only.\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`DuplicateKey.java`** \u2014 Added a `telephone(String)` helper that strips all non-digit characters (covering spaces, dashes and parentheses), returning `null` when the result is empty. This is the single source of truth for both storage and comparison.\n\n2. **`BuildOwner.java`** (POST) \u2014 After mapping the request, normalize the entity's telephone to digits-only, so the stored value (and the response, which is mapped from the entity) is digits-only.\n\n3. **`ApplyOwner.java`** (PUT) \u2014 Same normalization applied when updating an owner.\n\n4. **`CheckDuplicateOwner.java`** \u2014 Switched the uniqueness check from the whitespace/case `normalize` to the digit-stripping `telephone`, so the normalization is applied *before* comparison. `(613) 555-0100` and `6135550100` now collide \u2192 409 Conflict.\n\n5. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 Relaxed the `telephone` request pattern from `^[0-9]*$` to `^[-0-9() ]*$`. Without this, a formatted number was rejected with a 400 by bean validation before normalization could run. Digit-only responses still satisfy the pattern.\n\nBoth new `Cp11Tests` cases pass (`coreStoresDigitsOnly`, `functionalityNormalisedDuplicateRejected`), and no existing tests regressed.",
